wrong.  the amount of speed (whether what you call "speed" is 
amphetamine, methamphetamine, cathinone, methcathinone, or something
else) needed to get any effect is _way_ too high to actually put
on a blotter.  the ED50 (basically a measure of the effective dose)
for the "speed"y drugs i mentioned is:

    drug                  ED50 (mg/kg)
---------------           ------------
amphetamine                   0.71
cathinone                     0.71
methamphetamine               0.49
methcathinone                 0.37

reference: Glennon, R. A., M. Yousif, N. Naiman, and P. Kalix,
Methcathinone: A New and Potent Amphetamine-Like Agent, Pharmacology
Biochemistry and Behavior, 26, 547-551, 1987

so, for a typical adult male, weighing 170 lbs (77 kg), you'd need
anywhere from about 29 to 55 mg of the pure stuff to get an
effective dose.  ever try to put 30 mg of anything on a blotter?

the story that lsd is laced with "speed" is an urban myth, related
to the myth that lsd is laced with strychnine.  i refer you to
lengthy discussions on alt.drugs regarding these types of stories.
lsd itself can give rise to "speed"y like symptoms, which many
users mistake as being due to some contaminant (well, let me qualify
that, as some contaminants can cause more of these types of symptoms,
notably lsa, which arises from poor-quality extraction techniques).

i will admit that i've done both before (tripped and drank coffee).  
i think it's sort of a cool effect, especially when peaking.
caveat emptor: inexperienced people shouldn't try this.

